  "proposals": [
    {
      "title": "Keep the forecast on its native 0.1\u00b0 grid",
      "detail": "Open-Meteo is a 9 km model sampled every 0.1\u00b0. Painting it onto the 30 m analysis grid makes a regional forecast look like a village measurement. Store the coarse grid and let the tile reader resample it."
    },
    {
      "title": "Request 72 hours and label a stale feed",
      "detail": "The forecast asks for two days, so a 72-hour check has no array to read. Alerts already keep the last file when the API refuses; the radar clock should say the frame is saved rather than look live."
